            "review_title": "Review at Ngo Saigon Street Cafe Restaurant",
            "review_text": "babyceexx\nBirmingham, United Kingdom29 contributions\n1\nDisgraceful and would not recommend.\nNov 2018 • Family\nI am from the UK and came to Vietnam on holiday. My uncle and auntie who live in Saigon took me to this restaurant to dine in and spoke to the waitress in Vietnamese. I have a serve nut allergy and asked the waitress to have no nuts in one dish that I ordered. When served, the dish had nuts so instead of complaining I did not eat the dish. I ordered another dish and asked for no nuts. Again it came out with nuts, my uncle told the waitress I have a nut allergy and asked for the dish without the nuts. So the waitress took the dish and placed it on the table, called two other waitresses and stood there picking out the peanuts and handed the dish back to me. If I ate this dish I could die, the nuts have already been inside the dish and picking out 70% of the nuts is not going to stop me from reacting. Disgraceful considering my uncle spoke to them in Vietnamese so language wasn’t a barrier. The female waitress simply did not care\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 11, 2018\nLeKienLki\nHi babyceexx,\nFirstly, my company really apologize to you about this incident. Thank you for your feedback and contribution to our restaurants. I will send your comment to the manager to work with that restaurant as well as punishing, training his staffs and never let that situation happen again. Finally, my company apologize about this inconvenient situation and thank you for coming my restaurant. I hope you can have a beautiful experience in the next time. Thank you and have a good day.\nRead more\nWritten November 12, 2018\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
