            "review_title": "Review at Ngo Saigon Street Cafe Restaurant",
            "review_text": "DkL\nHo Chi Minh 40 contributions\n0\nVietnamese Street Food in the Mall.\nOct 2016 • Family\nThe restaurant is located at the famous Vincom Center food court. The menu design is beautiful and has wide range of local food that focus on Saigon street dishes (as the restaurant name). When we was there, the restaurant was packed with locals. We tried couple of local dishes such as Spring Rolls, Rice paper salad, grilled quail's egg pancake and the now famous Bun Cha. The price is very reasonable, we paid about 300K (about 13usd) for 2 of us including drinks. The restaurant is definitely good for people who want to try local food at air-con environment.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten November 14, 2016\nLeKienLki\nDear Sir,\n\nThanks for your review and delighted to hear that you have enjoyed our food and service. We hope to have a chance to serve you again soon.\n\nSincerely thanks!\nRead more\nWritten January 3, 2017\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
